  "notes": [
    "The grades are the owner's three buckets: 'desired' is the totem prefix, 'good' is the rest of the list, everything else is 'any'.",
    "The craft loop crosses rarities (a magic item from the transmute, a rare one from the regal), so the step filter reads only the classes and their grades; the slots describe the finished rare item.",
    "Tier numbers follow the data: the top tier of a family is the one with the highest required level. 'T1/T2 life' is IncreasedLife10 and IncreasedLife9, so it is exactly the two highest tiers.",
    "Slot one is the goal itself: the totem prefix must be there. A catch-all class in a slot would let any item satisfy the pattern, which is a step filter's job, not a goal's."
  ]
